title: DuFour Referendum campaign
subtitle: How should we campaign for the referendum?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: (impeachment_ref_time - 2) == rubicon_time
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/hindenburg_glaze_squadron.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
max-visits: 1

= DuFour Referendum campaign

With the referendum fast approaching, we have a chance to intensify our campaign and tip the scales in our favor. President DuFour’s health has deteriorated significantly since the last election, leaving him unable to participate—delegating the campaign effort to Trevannon and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span>. The <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ASPD**</span> have declared their full support for DuFour, while the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> backs him more quietly.

This fragmented and feeble campaign on the Right may offer us a chance to win through sheer voter turnout. That said, we must not grow complacent.

- @do_campaign: Let’s review our campaign options.
- @no_campaign: We shouldn't allocate resources to this.

@do_campaign

We have a variety of options to choose from.

- @propertied
- @prussia
- @reichsbanner
- @hope: We have done enough.
- @no_campaign_2: We shouldn't allocate resources to this.

@propertied
title: Set up an inter-party campaign committee with the Unity Coalition.
view-if: not banner_campaign_dufour
choose-if: impeachment_unionist and ((impeachment_ddp and not lvp_formed) or (impeachment_lvp and lvp_formed)) and unionist_relation >= 50 and ((ddp_relation >= 50 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation >= 50 and lvp_formed))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not impeachment_unionist: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> is not on our side. ?][? if not impeachment_ddp and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span> is not on our side. ?][? if not impeachment_lvp and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> is not on our side. ?][? if unionist_relation < 50 and impeachment_unionist: We need higher relations with the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>. ?][? if ddp_relation < 50 and impeachment_ddp: We need higher relations with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>. ?][? if lvp_relation < 50 and impeachment_lvp: We need higher relations with the <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>. ?]
on-arrival: pro_republic += 3; faithful_royalist -= 4; faithful_unionist += 3; faithful_marcher += 1; unionist_relation += 3; gold_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; ddp_left += 2; ddp_cohesion += 2; gold_left += 3; bourgeois_campaign_dufour = 1
face-image: img/weimar_coalition.jpg
go-to: do_campaign
max-visits: 1

The Unity Coalition has reunited to defend the very constitution we forged together—holding joint rallies and coordinating their messaging in a show of unity. This helps dismantle the Right’s narrative that the referendum is a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> power grab.

@prussia
title: We will utilize the Heartland government to discretely fund the campaign.
choose-if: marcher_heartland and (heartland_leader == "Pendrigon" or heartland_leader == "Bristol")
unavailable-subtitle: We are not in full control of Heartland.
on-arrival: commons_marcher += 4; burgher_marcher += 2; guild_marcher += 2; landed_marcher += 2; burgher_ddp += 2 if impeachment_ddp; guild_ddp += 2 if impeachment_ddp; burgher_gold += 2 if impeachment_gold; guild_gold += 2 if impeachment_gold; burgher_lvp += 4 if impeachment_lvp; guild_lvp += 4 if impeachment_lvp; commons_unionist += 2 if impeachment_unionist; burgher_unionist += 2 if impeachment_unionist; guild_unionist += 2 if impeachment_unionist; faithful_unionist += 2 if impeachment_unionist; pro_republic += 5; ddp_relation += 5; lvp_relation += 5; gold_relation += 5; unionist_relation += 5; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion += 1; heartland_campaign_dufour = 1; banner_militancy += 0.03; banner_strength += 100
face-image: img/weimar_coalition_3.jpg
go-to: do_campaign
max-visits: 1

We manage to funnel state funds into the coffers of the the Banners and various supporting <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> parties and organizations. Still, it pales in comparison to the mountains of silver and gold flowing to DuFour from the Commonwealth Army.

@reichsbanner
title: It’s time for the the Banners to get a little more <i>active</i>.
subtitle: -2 resource
view-if: not bourgeois_campaign_dufour
choose-if: resources >= 2 and knight_strength >= reformist_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2: Not enough resources. ?][? if knight_strength < reformist_strength: The Neorevisionist faction needs to be more powerful than the Reformists. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; banner_strength += 150; banner_militancy += 0.1; loyalist_strength *= 0.9; warden_strength *= 0.9; commons_royalist -= 2; commons_marcher += 4; disfavored_royalist -= 4; disfavored_marcher += 6; burgher_marcher += 2; guild_marcher -= 4; landed_marcher -= 4; faithful_marcher -= 4; pro_republic -= 5; unionist_relation -= 10; ddp_relation -= 10; gold_relation -= 10; lvp_relation -= 10; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 3; ddp_cohesion -= 3; banner_campaign_dufour = 1
face-image: img/reichsbanner_2.jpg
go-to: do_campaign
max-visits: 1

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> have harassed us long enough—it’s time to strike back. The propertied parties are criticizing us turning the the Banners into a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> militia.

@hope
view-if: bourgeois_campaign_dufour or heartland_campaign_dufour or bourgeois_campaign_dufour

We can only hope for the best.

@no_campaign_2
view-if: not bourgeois_campaign_dufour and not heartland_campaign_dufour and not bourgeois_campaign_dufour
on-arrival: commons_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 3; commons_royalist += 3; burgher_royalist += 3; guild_royalist += 3; pro_republic -= 5; faithful_marcher -= 2; faithful_royalist += 2; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_marcher -= 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; disfavored_collectivist += 3

With or without a strong campaign, we believe the wave of support we gained after toppling Staal’s regime will be enough to carry us to victory in the referendum. The Right remains too fractured to fully exploit our relative absence from the field—though we’ve begun to notice a troubling uptick in opposition activity, with expenses being covered by an unknown source.

@no_campaign
on-arrival: commons_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 3; commons_royalist += 3; burgher_royalist += 3; guild_royalist += 3; pro_republic -= 5; faithful_marcher -= 2; faithful_royalist += 2; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_marcher -= 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; disfavored_collectivist += 3

With or without a strong campaign, we believe the wave of support we gained after toppling Staal’s regime will be enough to carry us to victory in the referendum. The Right remains too fractured to fully exploit our relative absence from the field—though we’ve begun to notice a troubling uptick in opposition activity, with expenses being covered by an unknown source.